  "authored_after": "agent-112 request 8015135d. In the running matched campaign (ff0fe1c/v8), db-coverage.baseline.s0 and candidate.s0 both ran make test-integration successfully against disposable PostgreSQL. Baseline then deleted .integration-ran and v8 graded it incomplete. v1-v8 and campaign reports stay unchanged.",
  "reason": "The marker file is neither necessary nor sufficient: it can be cleaned up after a real run, or fabricated. v9 grades real database execution from the harness-recorded command output (initdb provisioning, an ok for the package, no FAIL/SKIP/cached/panic) with the integration target, script and DB test still intact. Adding a tie-break regression test is reported separately as a descriptive dimension, not as the outcome. The command must actually invoke the integration target (anchored at the start of a shell segment, so echoing its name does not count), and the output must contain initdb's own messages and Go's timed ok line.",
